Read your named assignments/batchN.record. It supplies exactly the newly captured
native screenshots you own. Read every assigned image ONCE through view_image,
at most 8 images total, no other images, crops, resizing, browser or rerender.
You have no image-bearing history. Parent does not reopen these images.
You are not alone in this checkout; do not modify or revert anyone else's work.
Your only write scope is observations/results/batchN.record and optional scratch
code alongside that result. Use apply_patch for manual edits.

This is visual display review only, not mathematical/source/key review.
All content, choices and figures are already independently approved, and the
runtime's exact text, SVG, coverage, scrolling, fonts and offline checks passed.
Observe actual pixels for unreadable text, missing-glyph squares, wrong formula
layout, unexpected overlap, malformed rows, or clipped content that cannot be
reached. These are native viewport scroll positions, so normal content continuing
above/below the viewport, or a horizontally scrollable mathematical line at a
nonzero scroll position, is not itself a defect. Do not claim offscreen pixels
were seen. Record specific visible observations for each actual image.

Return JSON in observations/results/batchN.record:
{
  "status": "DISPLAY_PASS" or "DISPLAY_REVISE",
  "blockers": [],
  "images": [
    {
      "path": "<exact assignment absolute image path>",
      "sha256": "<exact verified SHA256>",
      "observations": ["specific visible content/layout observations"],
      "blockers": []
    }
  ],
  "imageAccounting": {
    "views": <actual>, "uniqueImages": <actual>,
    "reopens": 0, "crops": 0, "resizes": 0, "rerenders": 0
  },
  "parentImages": 0, "databaseWrites": 0, "finish": "review",
  "hostTokens": "unknown", "totalCost": "unknown"
}

Use DISPLAY_PASS only after all assigned images were actually observed with no
blocking display defect. A failed image tool call is not an observation; preserve
its actual failure and report it. Compute the result SHA and return only a compact
text result with batch ID, status, output absolute path, SHA and image count.
Do not send image payloads, message other chats, commit, push, create/attach a
worktree, mutate content, write DB, merge or deploy.
